Research Technician
Edinburgh - Kings Buildings, Midlothian, United Kingdom

&nbsp;

Grade UE06: £35,302 - £40,704&nbsp;per annum

College of Science and Engineering / School of Chemistry&nbsp;

Full-time: 35 hours&nbsp;per week

Fixed-term: for 48 months&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The Opportunity:

Where discovery never stops. Be part of something bigger.&nbsp;

This position will involve working as part of an exciting new UK and international team to discover novel features of bacterial lipid chemistry. As well as your own research focus, you will also be part of something bigger — where your work has real impact and your development matters. As a research technician your role will be essential to supporting broader research in Edinburgh, and the smooth operation of our facilities. Whether you're maintaining cutting-edge lab equipment, facilitating ground-breaking research, developing new techniques, or enhancing student and staff experience with top-notch facilities, your work will have a lasting impact that stretches far beyond our academic community.

You will carry out research on your own specific targets, as well as supporting data acquisition and management across the consortium members. You will also play a key role in managing research meetings for both the PIs and PDRAs employed on the project, acting as the essential link across the lifetime of this long-term study. We are a place where everyone is welcome and offer a range of policies and benefits designed to support you in building the right meaningful flexibility that works for you. This role will provide interesting and exciting work, opportunities for publication, variety every day and responsibility and autonomy. We look forward to you joining one of the world’s leading universities.&nbsp;

